  "slug": "cryo-structure-34d6",
  "summary": "Generative ensemble models, rare-event fingerprints and solvation-aware potentials are reframing structure prediction as sampling distributions with energetics.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread treats biomolecules as conformational distributions with attached energetics rather than single poses. OriDynamics proposes a unified all-atom generative framework for protein monomers and complexes with ligands or partners; REVEAL chains generative secondary-structure sampling, trRosettaRNA2 tertiary prediction, unbiased MD and Markov state modeling for HIV-1 TAR RNA; transition-conditioned dynamical fingerprints rank microscopic participants inside a transition corridor for rare A-B events. A second strand embeds physics in learned representations: HEIWA injects explicit-implicit solvent attention into ESM3 embeddings, AIMNet2-CPCM evaluates solvated ligand strain across roughly 8K PDB ligands, EvoPhi-DDG is averaged with JanusDDG under antisymmetry constraints, and StableProt fuses Foldseek 3Di tokens with SaProt for calibrated Tm/OGT. Design and docking work is more guarded: ProTEUS and PAMP close mutation-resolved loops to all-atom or turnover objectives, while focused torsional supervision gave no DiffDock gain and Pyrite benchmarks agentic cofold pose ranking.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-12"
}
